HST Office: the HASON TECH banner fits snugly: its slot is exactly its artwork, on the ribbon, in the Start Center
and wherever else it is shown (owner, 19/11/2026: no letterbox, no filler band, no padding).

- include/vcl/HstBannerGeometry.hxx: widthForHeight, heightForWidth; snugSlot (the part of a host's room that holds
  the artwork exactly: the room's height, the artwork's ratio, at the room's left or right edge); artRect (the
  artwork is painted over the whole allocation when it has the artwork's ratio, fitted only until a host has
  resized the slot for a new artwork).
- vcl HstBannerCore: the artwork is painted without the 3 px inset and without the 1.0.3 ribbon's filler (the
  colour of the artwork's right edge over the rest of the slot); the core reports the shown artwork's size
  (ArtSize) and tells its view when a new artwork has another ratio (BannerArtChanged); the standard size it asks
  the feed for follows the room the host offers (BannerRoomWidth), not the narrower slot.
- vcl HstRibbonBanner: Place(rRoom, bAnchorLeft) keeps the room and takes its snug slot in it, again when the
  artwork's ratio changes; WidthForHeight for hosts. The rest of the room is the host's own background.
- vcl HstBannerWidget: HeightForWidth (the contract of hosts that size the slot themselves, with SetArtChangedHdl);
  the drawing area asks for the artwork's height at the width it was given, so the Start Center's slot is sized to
  the image, not the image to the slot.
- sfx2 NotebookbarTabControl: the Tabbed ribbon's banner room is unchanged (360 to 960 logical px, 96 high, from
  8 px after the last group to 8 px before the window's right edge); the banner takes its artwork's width flush
  with the room's right end (owner, 19/11/2026), so it stands at the same place on every tab and the free room
  between the last group and the banner is the ribbon's own background. The groups' fit is unchanged. With gtk and
  qt only the page paints the body, and the page stops before the room: the room is now painted in the body's
  colour (the window colour, as the other toolkits' tab control paints its whole panel), so the body is one
  surface behind the banner instead of a step after the last group.

